= Weighted mean

Two lab sessions measured the same quantity. The first recorded
two readings with a mean of 12. The second recorded three with a mean of 17.

== Combine the readings

Weight each session mean by its number of readings, then divide by
the total number of readings.

$ (2 times 12 + 3 times 17) / (2 + 3) = 15 $

The combined mean of the five readings is 15.
